# Modular Family Controllers & Swagger Separation Architecture

## 1. Executive Summary & Objective

### Requirement:
> *"@[src/family] now all do divided separate by like memories will and invite will be separate and title will have"*

### Solution Overview:
Previously, all endpoints inside `src/family/` were lumped together inside a single massive `FamilyController` file under one generic `@ApiTags('Family Sanctuary')`. In Swagger UI, this caused over 25 different endpoints (Memories, Invitations, Members, Relationships, Documents, Events, Settings) to appear squished together under a single section.

We have restructured the `src/family/` module into **7 distinct, single-responsibility controllers**, each with its own descriptive **Swagger Title & OpenAPI Tag**:
1. **`MemoriesController`** &rarr; `@ApiTags('Memories Vault')`
2. **`InvitationsController`** &rarr; `@ApiTags('Family Invitations')`
3. **`MembersController`** &rarr; `@ApiTags('Family Members')`
4. **`RelationshipsController`** &rarr; `@ApiTags('Family Relationships')`
5. **`EventsController`** &rarr; `@ApiTags('Family Events')`
6. **`DocumentsController`** &rarr; `@ApiTags('Documents Archive')`
7. **`FamilyController`** &rarr; `@ApiTags('Family Sanctuary')`

All controllers share the underlying `FamilyService`, maintaining zero regression and 100% backward compatibility with all frontend routes.

---

## 2. Controller Breakdown & Swagger Sections

### A. Memories Vault (`memories.controller.ts`)
- **Swagger Tag**: `Memories Vault`
- **Route Prefix**: `/family/memories`
- **Endpoints**:
  - `GET /family/memories` – Retrieve user-isolated memories gallery
  - `GET /family/memories/:id` – Fetch a single memory by ID
  - `POST /family/memories` – Create a new memory story with photos, dates, and locations
  - `PATCH /family/memories/:id` – Update an existing memory
  - `DELETE /family/memories/:id` – Remove a memory from the vault

### B. Family Invitations (`invitations.controller.ts`)
- **Swagger Tag**: `Family Invitations`
- **Route Prefix**: `/family/invitations`
- **Endpoints**:
  - `GET /family/invitations` – Retrieve list of pending member invitations
  - `POST /family/invitations` – Send a new family invite request
  - `PATCH /family/invitations/:id` – Approve or reject join request

### C. Family Members (`members.controller.ts`)
- **Swagger Tag**: `Family Members`
- **Route Prefix**: `/family/members`
- **Endpoints**:
  - `GET /family/members` – Retrieve all family members in sanctuary
  - `GET /family/members/search` – Search member profiles for deduplication & relative linking
  - `POST /family/members` – Add a new family relative or link existing profile
  - `PATCH /family/members/:id` – Update member profile
  - `DELETE /family/members/:id` – Remove member from sanctuary

### D. Family Relationships & Lineage (`relationships.controller.ts`)
- **Swagger Tag**: `Family Relationships`
- **Route Prefix**: `/family/relationships`
- **Endpoints**:
  - `GET /family/relationships` – Retrieve family tree relationships graph matrix
  - `POST /family/relationships` – Create relationship link between two relatives

### E. Family Events (`events.controller.ts`)
- **Swagger Tag**: `Family Events`
- **Route Prefix**: `/family/events`
- **Endpoints**:
  - `GET /family/events` – Retrieve upcoming events, reunions, and birthdays
  - `POST /family/events` – Schedule a new event

### F. Documents Archive (`documents.controller.ts`)
- **Swagger Tag**: `Documents Archive`
- **Route Prefix**: `/family/documents`
- **Endpoints**:
  - `GET /family/documents` – Retrieve encrypted documents archive
  - `POST /family/documents` – Upload single or bundle documents
  - `POST /family/documents/multiple` – Upload batch documents
  - `DELETE /family/documents/:id` – Delete a single document
  - `DELETE /family/documents` – Delete all documents

### G. Family Sanctuary (`family.controller.ts`)
- **Swagger Tag**: `Family Sanctuary`
- **Route Prefix**: `/family`
- **Endpoints**:
  - `GET /family/sanctuary` – Main family overview & statistics
  - `PATCH /family/update` – Update sanctuary family name & description
  - `PATCH /family/settings` – Update sanctuary preferences
  - `GET /family/activity` – Audit activity logs
  - `GET /family/admin/stats` – Administrative network statistics

---

## 3. Module Registration (`family.module.ts`)

All controllers are registered inside [family.module.ts](file:///d:/Projects/family-together-backend/src/family/family.module.ts):
```typescript
@Module({
  imports: [PrismaModule, MailModule],
  controllers: [
    FamilyController,
    MembersController,
    RelationshipsController,
    MemoriesController,
    EventsController,
    DocumentsController,
    InvitationsController,
  ],
  providers: [FamilyService],
  exports: [FamilyService],
})
export class FamilyModule {}
```

---

## 4. Key Benefits

1. **Swagger UI Readability**: Distinct sections with clear visual titles make testing and exploring APIs intuitive.
2. **Clean Separation of Concerns**: Each controller file is under 100 lines and focused solely on its domain.
3. **Zero Frontend Regressions**: All URLs, HTTP verbs, query parameters, and JSON payloads remain identical.
